[[File:E 016.png|thumb|[[Assassin Bear|Assassin Bear]], the first example of a Dark enemy]]
'''Dark Enemies''' (Japanese: 黒い敵 ''Kuroi Teki'', '''Black Enemies''') are a type of [[Enemy Units|Enemy Unit]]. Most of them are rusher-type enemies that can be knocked back easily, but have high health, rapid attacks, massive damage output, low range, and fast movement speed, with a few exceptions. They usually rely on raw stats rather than [[Special Abilities|special abilities]]. Later-introduced Dark enemies tend to be immune to freeze, including [[Masked Okame]], [[Chocolate Doge]], [[Dark Wind]] and the Dark [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoths]]. The first Dark enemy, [[Assassin Bear]], can be found in the [[Higher Score|Challenge Battle]] after finishing [[Empire of Cats]] Chapter 1.

See [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|here]] for a list of units with anti-Dark abilities.

*The [[Ototo Corps|Iron Wall Foundation]] reduces the damage all [[Cat Units]] take from Dark enemies by 0.75% per level up to a maximum of 15%.
*Dark enemies are associated with Purple [[Catfruit]], which can be obtained from the [[Growing Catfruit]] stage [[Violet Flash]].
*Anti-Dark abilities are improved by the [[Void Fruit]] from [[Into the Future]].
*Dark [[Talent Orbs]] can be obtained from the following stages:
**[[Enigma Stages]]: [[Cradle Shrine (Deadly)/Dark|Dark Cradle]], [[Summit Shrine (Merciless)/Dark|Dark Summit]], [[Frontier Shrine (Merciless)/Dark|Dark Frontier]]
**[[Island of Hidden Treasure]]: [[Ebony Dawn]], [[Ebony Apex]], [[Ebony Refuge]]
**[[Le'Grim Strikes]] [[Continuation Stage]]s: [[Le'Grim Strikes/Cradle Wilderness (Deadly)|Cradle Wilderness]], [[Le'Grim Strikes/Summit Wilderness (Merciless)|Summit Wilderness]], [[Le'Grim Strikes/Frontier Wilderness (Merciless)|Frontier Wilderness]]

==Trivia==
*The Dark trait's English name was Black before being changed in [[Version 15.3 Update|Version 15.3]] for unknown reasons. This development was not reflected in all other main versions of the game.
**Several Dark enemies and stages/maps containing them were renamed accordingly in 15.3, including Gory Black ([[Gory Dark]]), Black Cyclone ([[Dark Cyclone]]), Black Okame ([[Masked Okame]]), Black Wind ([[Dark Wind]]), Black Premonition ([[Dark Premonition]]), Black Citadel ([[Dark Citadel]]), Black Cradle ([[Dark Cradle]]), Black Summit ([[Dark Summit]]), Black Frontier ([[Dark Frontier]]) and VS Team Black ([[VS Team Dark ①|VS Team Dark]]). [[Version 15.5 Update|Version 15.5]] also renamed Dark Cyclone's stages, changing "B-Cyclone" to "D-Cyclone".
***[[Bun Bun Black]] and [[Black Slug]] were unchanged, and some other enemies' names still contain different languages' words for black: [[Director Kurosawah]] and [[Crocodylidae Kurocroc]] have ''kuro'' (Japanese for black), while [[Le'noir]] has ''noir'' (French for black).
**As a result of this change, several non-Dark enemies' names are now misleading, including [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]], [[Dark Emperor Santa]], all enemy [[Axe Cat (Normal Cat)|Dark Cat]] variants and [[Dark Priest Mamon]].
**Some of the original names can still be seen in [[The Battle Cats POP!]].
*Many Dark enemies are associated with deadliness, assassination, stealth or espionage. [[Assassin Bear]] and the enemy [[:Category:Killer Cats|Killer Cats]] have "Assassin" or "Killer" in their names, [[Doge Dark]] is a part-time killer, [[Shadow Boxer K]]'s English and Japanese descriptions both mention murder, [[Tackey]]'s Japanese description says its curveballs are deadly, [[Razorback]]'s Japanese description claims he was stained by evil, becomes more violent when something happens to his hair, and debuts in [[The Spy Who Pet Me]] (a spoof of [[wikipedia:The Spy Who Loved Me (novel)|''The Spy Who Loved Me'']]), [[Crocodylidae Kurocroc]] tried out stealth camping, and [[Perry Duche]] is referred to as "a new assassin" (新たな刺客) in the announcement for the [[Anniversary/12 1/2 Year|12th and 1/2 Anniversary]]'s expanded version of [[Road to Unification]]. [[Betakkuma (Rare Cat)|Black Betakkuma]] and [[Nekokkuma (Special Cat)|Killer Nekokkuma]] also follow this theme with their description and name respectively, but do not appear as enemies.
**Doge Dark's description implies that he was trained by Assassin Bear after finding one of his distributed flyers, and likewise for Black Betakkuma's Taiwanese description.
*Since [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] and [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] were the only enemy types in [[Ganso!! Nyanko Daisensou]], Assassin Bear was originally considered a Traitless enemy. Many future Dark enemies took inspiration from his design.
*In [[Nyanko Defence Force]], [[Jackie Peng]] had Red, Dark and [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] variants that have not appeared in other games.
*In [[Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarou: Youkai Dotabata Daisensou|YuruGeGe]], the [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/t/%A4%D8%A4%E9%A4%AF%A4%EC%A4%B9 Hercules enemies] filled a similar role to Dark enemies, typically having very high speed and higher damage compared to their original variants.
